  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "From what I can tell a lot of people sorta think $10 is a bit high and should be reduced to around $5, and those are just my English speaking friends from countries like America and the UK. For people from other countries with a lower income, it sure would be helpful if the price would be lower cause for a lot of people $10 is actually quite a lot of money. For example, someone told me $10 would cover their bus tickets to work and back for around 2 weeks which is crazy when I think $10 will only last me two days ticket money even with a student discount. So Perhaps pulling geographical location from players Steam account, method of payment(where their credit card is from) or simply by using their IP address to give appropriate pricing to the end-user would be a step in the right direction.",
